## Judgment 1: projection honesty — HOLDS
  env.ts: `harnessEnv` builds a new `{}` and loops the module-local `Object.freeze`d 10-name array, reading
    `parent[name]` and copying it only when the value is not undefined. It never writes to `parent`. There is no
    regex, no prefix and no case folding, and the list matches the brief's names exactly.
  Review-checked constraints: `harnessEnv` is imported only by claude-code.ts and codex.ts.
    harness/index.ts and src/index.ts do not re-export it (rg harnessEnv|harness/env over packages/apps/adapters).
  All four spawn expressions project: claude-code.ts:113 runClaude `env: harnessEnv(opts.env)`, claude-code.ts:148
    available() `env: harnessEnv(process.env)`, codex.ts:144 runCodex `harnessEnv(opts.env)`, codex.ts:196
    available() `{ env: harnessEnv(process.env) }`.
  Census: I grepped every non-test child_process importer and every spawn/spawnSync/exec*/fork call in
    packages, apps, adapters and scripts. Outside the shim's harness, no call spawns claude or codex:
    - providers/src/index.ts:181 runs the fixed `npx --yes quota-axi`. quotaAxiSource({}) is its only caller
      (cli/providers.ts:51).
    - commands/ci.ts:117 runs the fixed CI_STEPS npm lines.
    - commands/run.ts:213 and commands/lifecycle.ts:476 (`red`) run operator argv.
    - pipeline/index.ts:78 runs probatio commands.
    - cli/close.ts:49 runs `bash docs/design/dossier/build.sh`. That script mentions claude only in comment URLs.
    - shim fake.ts:34 runs process.execPath on its own script.
    - The rest are git and treehouse helpers, plus bin/bisellium.mjs, which runs node.
    Outside harness/, no `"claude"` or `"codex"` string literal is used as a spawn argument.
  Advisory, out of scope per the brief: quota-axi runs with the full ambient env. It is a third-party CLI, not a
    vendor harness, and the brief excludes providers explicitly.

## Judgment 2: per-entry-path mapping — FAIL (F1, one class, three instances)
  Behaviours 1–3 are exact. After each direct call they assert the cumulative log.length (1, 2, then 3), which is
  equivalent to taking a snapshot before each call. Behaviour 4 is not exact:
  F1a harness-env.test.ts:393 `seg1 = log.slice(0, 2)`. The partition is a fixed offset. Nothing asserts that the
      first runTalk added exactly 2 records. The brief says: "takes the log's length immediately before each call,
      and partitions the records that call added".
  F1b harness-env.test.ts:412 `seg2 = log.slice(2, 4)`. Same gap for the second runTalk. The tick's `slice(4)` is
      also a fixed offset, but its total-count assertion keeps it exact only because the phases before it are.
  F1c harness-env.test.ts:449-452. Every tick pair accepts `start` OR `resume of sess-w049`. The brief says: "A
      magister whose session file exists resumes `sess-w049`; every other magister starts." Here eng-lead holds the
      only session file, so the tick should produce exactly one resume and four starts.
  Consequence: two mutations survive the FULL `npm test` (npm test exit=0 under each):
    M13  talk.ts `existing && existing.harness === harnessId` -> `... && params.modelOnly !== undefined`
         (the tick path never resumes). The phase probe shows tick = 5× [version, turn:start], so eng-lead starts
         even though it holds a session. Suite: PASS=1919, FAIL=0.
    M15  runTalk path only: the first call launches an extra `--version` after its start, and a call with a session
         file skips its probe. The phase probe shows runTalk #1 = [version, turn:start, version] and runTalk #2 =
         [turn:resume]. That is an extra vendor launch in one call, masked by an omission in the next. It is the
         aggregate-vs-exact case the brief names ("an extra vendor launch"). It is contrived, two coordinated
         edits, but it survives only because no per-call count exists. Suite: PASS=1916, FAIL=0.
    M08b (a double start in performTalk) is killed. Its first FAIL is attributed to the SECOND runTalk
         ("second runTalk logs exactly [version, turn] ["turn","version"]"), which shows the offset partition at work.
  The brief's censor mutations are all killed (three-suite driver below; each KILLED line has a non-zero exit):
    M01 +ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL | M02 startsWith | M03 regex | M04 case-insensitive | M05 LC_/NODE_ pattern |
    M06a–d drop harnessEnv at each of the four spawn expressions | M07 delete from parent in place | M06c doubles as
    "opts.env through for codex only" | M08a start twice (profile) | M08b/M08c start/resume twice (performTalk) |
    M09a/b/c skip the available() probe (always / tick only / when a session exists) | M10 inject a default for an
    absent name | M11a/b W-044 M24/M25 against A1 | M12a random stub session_id against A2 | M12b resume a
    different id. M14 (the tick resumes sess-w049 for every magister) is killed ONLY by talk-boundary's `sess-stub`
    literal. harness-env's behaviour 4 passes it: F1c again.
  Remedy (all three instances in one round, harness-env.test.ts only):
    R1  Before each of the three behaviour-4 calls, take `before = readLog(logPath).length`. Assert that the call
        added exactly 2 records (each runTalk) or exactly 2 × dailies written (tick), and partition by
        `slice(before)`.
    R2  Tick form: assert the resume/start mapping. A resume of sess-w049 is expected iff the magister's
        `sessions/<sella>.json` existed before runTick (here exactly one resume, eng-lead) and a start otherwise.
        Asserting "exactly one resume and four starts", with the expected count derived from the session files
        present before the tick, is enough.
    Must-kill against harness-env.test.ts ALONE: M13, M14, M15. The driver and phase probe below reproduce them.
  The same class exists in talk-boundary.test.ts, which predates this opus and falls outside its declared edits
  ("stub log path, A1, A2 only"), so fixing it is not required here:
    :246 behaviour 1 destructures [start, resume] and asserts only that both are defined, not exactly 2.
    :341 the tick form is inferred from the argv, so start or resume is accepted for any magister (M13 also
      survives this file).
    I recommend filing these separately, or folding them into W-054/W-046 at the architect's call.
  Searched: every slice(, log.length and .length === line, plus every start/resume form inference, in
  harness-env.test.ts and talk-boundary.test.ts. harness.test.ts counts no spawns. ci.test.ts's stub logs npm,
  not a vendor binary.

