## Judgment 4: attended smoke — SCRUB HALF PROVEN LIVE (pass); allow half recorded
  Temp copy of examples/sample-studio in my scratchpad (never studio/). The canaries were exported in MY shell:
    ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9 ANTHROPIC_MODEL=zz-w049-bogus npm run -s bisellium -- talk --sella eng-lead
    --model-only --studio <copy> "Run bisellium context --sella eng-lead --studio <copy> and report its exit code and
    first line."
  Result: talk exit=0, run 03:37:32Z–03:37:41Z. A real reply arrived (786 chars). timeline/eng-lead.jsonl has in
    and out records with a sessionId, and usage {input:4, output:566}. The receipt's exitCode is 0. Neither canary
    string appears anywhere in the studio copy.
  Positive controls, so the pass isn't vacuous. I ran `claude -p` directly (no bisellium, no scrub) with one
  canary each:
    A  ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9 hit the timeout (exit 124) with no reply.
    B  ANTHROPIC_MODEL=zz-w049-bogus got is_error=true, api_error_status=404 ("issue with the selected model
       (zz-w049-bogus)"), exit 1.
    So either canary, had it reached the child, would have prevented a reply. The talked turn's reply proves both
    were scrubbed. The controls' requests went only to a dead localhost port or to the real vendor with a bogus
    model name, so nothing leaked.
  The brief's second pass condition (timeline `model` != zz-w049-bogus) is VACUOUS as written. The timeline `model`
    is absent for real claude turns: claude-code.ts maps `model: parsed.model`, but the real `-p --output-format
    json` envelope carries `modelUsage`, not a top-level `model`. The receipt has no model either. This predates
    W-049 and is out of its scope. I recommend filing it. The controls above stand in for it.
  Allow half (baseline for W-054): the session did not reach `bisellium context`. Its first call was bare
    `bisellium`, which the boot bundle's "CLI usage" rule tells it to run before any CLI call. That call was denied
    under dontAsk, so the session reports no exit code: neither 0 nor 127, but "denied". This is a separate
    observation for W-054/W-044's owner. The boot bundle's usage rule conflicts with the talked session's admitted
    verbs.
  The operator's login is valid. The prior attempt's 401 (expired OAuth) no longer reproduces.

## Judgment 5: instance-or-class, and leak greps
  F1 is one class (behaviour 4's spawn map is aggregate/offset-based rather than exact per call) with three
    instances, F1a/F1b/F1c, all enumerated above. The two pre-existing talk-boundary instances are listed separately.
  F2 (single instance): docs/ADOPTION.md, "Running talk", says "(`harnessEnv`, `@bisellium/shim`)". That wording
    reads as a public export, which contradicts the brief's review-checked constraint that harnessEnv is NOT
    re-exported. Name the module (`packages/shim/src/harness/env.ts`) instead. I grepped for harnessEnv across
    docs/: this is the only mention.
  Value greps. Patterns: the 40 SYNTH sentinel values (`SYNTH-<name>-VALUE`, the proxy sentinel), plus the values
  of every ANTHROPIC_*, CLAUDE_*, CLAUDECODE, OPENAI_* and proxy var in my shell that is 6 or more chars long.
  Only counts were printed.
    - Branch logs (7 files under studio/ci added by the range): sentinel hits 0. The real-value hits come only from
      CLAUDE_TMPDIR and CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR, a 16-char path equal to the sandbox temp root: 01.log ×1 and 04.log
      ×10. Masked context shows mkdtemp paths (the system-prompt file in argv details, and tick's "wrote …/acta/…"
      lines), i.e. os.tmpdir() output. It is not an env echo and not a secret, so this is a false positive of the
      grep and not a leak.
    - My own outputs (the pre-fix reds, the mutation runs, step 2): sentinel hits 0. This log: see the tail.
  Positive control on the grep: all 4 reds contain the NAME `SYNTH`, and the guard NAME ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL appears
    in reds 01–04 (2/1/3/14), so the grep had material to match against.

